  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "GTiffDataset::ReadStrile",
    "file": "gdal/gdal/frmts/gtiff/geotiff.cpp",
    "description": "GTiffDataset::ReadStrile passes nBlockReqSize directly to TIFFReadEncodedTile(). For malformed TIFFs, the requested output size can be larger than the actual raw tile data loaded by TIFFFillTile; in COMPRESSION_NONE path this reaches DumpModeDecode(), which blindly memcpy()s from tif->tif_rawcp after only checking tif->tif_rawcc < cc. Here tif->tif_rawcp points to an invalid/wild mapped source region, causing a wild read in _TIFFmemcpy at tif_dumpmode.c:101.",
    "conditions": "Fuzzer opens a crafted tiled GTiff (COMPRESSION_NONE / dump mode decode path) with inconsistent tile metadata (tile byte count/offset/content) such that GTiffDataset::LoadBlockBuf computes a block request size and ReadStrile calls TIFFReadEncodedTile with that size, while libtiff raw tile pointer/available bytes do not describe a valid readable source buffer. During raster read (IReadBlock -> ReadStrile -> TIFFReadEncodedTile -> DumpModeDecode), _TIFFmemcpy(buf, tif->tif_rawcp, cc) dereferences an invalid source pointer and crashes."
  },
